``` Xen Orchestra Authentication Bypass (VSA-2026-062) Exploited to Take Over XCP-ng Hosts
    Field names follow CIM/UDM conventions and have not been tested against live data; adjust them to your environment.
    Splunk hunt, CIM data models (tstats) plus raw log searches for behaviours. Author: daniyyell-dev. https://github.com/daniyyell-dev/rapid-threat-intel/tree/main/threats/2026-11_November-2026/2026-11-11/Xen-Orchestra-VSA-2026-062-Auth-Bypass-XCP-ng-Takeover
    Sources: https://docs.vates.tech/security-advisories/advisories/2026/vates-sa-2026-062/ ; https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/hackers-exploit-critical-xen-orchestra.html
    Published 2026-11-10. Set the time picker to at least the last 30 days, or back to the earliest activity in the sources.
    The indicators below are live and malicious: do not browse to them.
    Needs these CIM data models populated: Network_Traffic, Web, Endpoint. A model with no data simply returns nothing.
    summariesonly=false also reads events the acceleration has not summarised yet. If these data models are
    accelerated, summariesonly=true is much faster but only sees the summary range.
    No CIM? Use hunt_raw.spl with the rti_* macros from all/splunk_macros.conf.
    Output: first_seen, last_seen, ioc, ioc_type, data_model, host, user, src, dest, detail, count

    Behaviours (indicators of attack) are extra sections below, with ioc_type "behaviour (alert)" or "behaviour (hunt)".
    Behaviours are leads, not confirmed indicators, and can match legitimate activity. Compare any hit against your own baseline and environment before acting.
    Behaviours are for hunting and alerting only; never block on them.
    Sections that read raw logs use index=*: replace it with your own index names to make them faster. ```
| tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
    FROM datamodel=Network_Traffic.All_Traffic
    WHERE All_Traffic.dest_ip IN ("91.211.251.112", "193.148.56.72", "37.221.208.216", "45.66.35.11", "64.65.0.120", "64.65.62.160", "89.47.51.90", "92.60.37.247")
    BY All_Traffic.src_ip All_Traffic.dest_ip All_Traffic.dest_port All_Traffic.action All_Traffic.dvc All_Traffic.user
| rename "All_Traffic.*" AS *
| eval data_model="Network_Traffic", ioc_type="ipv4", ioc=dest_ip, host=dvc, src=src_ip, dest=dest_ip, detail="connection to IOC, port ".dest_port.", ".action
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Network_Traffic.All_Traffic
        WHERE All_Traffic.src_ip IN ("91.211.251.112", "193.148.56.72", "37.221.208.216", "45.66.35.11", "64.65.0.120", "64.65.62.160", "89.47.51.90", "92.60.37.247")
        BY All_Traffic.src_ip All_Traffic.dest_ip All_Traffic.dest_port All_Traffic.action All_Traffic.dvc All_Traffic.user
    | rename "All_Traffic.*" AS *
    | eval data_model="Network_Traffic", ioc_type="ipv4", ioc=src_ip, host=dvc, src=src_ip, dest=dest_ip, detail="connection from IOC, port ".dest_port.", ".action
]

``` Behaviour 1 (Alert): Auth-bypass cookie sent to Xen Orchestra
    Look for: HTTP requests to Xen Orchestra with the cookie authenticationToken=j:{} or authenticationToken=j:%7B%7D
    Log source: Reverse-proxy, WAF or packet capture in front of Xen Orchestra
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Web.Web
        WHERE Web.cookie="*authenticationToken=j:*"
        BY Web.src Web.user Web.dest Web.url Web.http_user_agent Web.status
    | rename "Web.*" AS *
    | eval host=dest, detail="HTTP ".status." ".url." UA: ".http_user_agent, data_model="Web"
    | eval ioc="Auth-bypass cookie sent to Xen Orchestra", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 2 (Hunt): Login-token harvesting requests
    Look for: Requests to /rest/v0/users/me/authentication_tokens from unfamiliar addresses
    Log source: Reverse-proxy and web logs
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Web.Web
        WHERE Web.url="*/rest/v0/users/me/authentication_tokens*"
        BY Web.src Web.user Web.dest Web.url Web.http_user_agent Web.status
    | rename "Web.*" AS *
    | eval host=dest, detail="HTTP ".status." ".url." UA: ".http_user_agent, data_model="Web"
    | eval ioc="Login-token harvesting requests", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]

``` Behaviour 3 (Alert): Attacker foothold VM on XCP-ng
    Look for: A VM named pivot2, VMs with hvm_serial: file, or '-serial file:' in /var/log/xensource.log
    Log source: XCP-ng hosts (xe vm-list, xensource.log), syslog
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* ("-serial file:" OR "pivot2" OR "hvm_serial")
    | eval host=host, user=coalesce(user, "-"), src=coalesce(src, src_ip, "-"), dest=sourcetype, detail=substr(replace(_raw, "\s+", " "), 1, 300)
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="XCP-ng logs"
    | eval ioc="Attacker foothold VM on XCP-ng", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 4 (Alert): Persistence files on XCP-ng hosts
    Look for: Files /etc/cron.d/zz-ustar, /etc/cron.d/zz-ustar2, /.ustar5, /.ustar6, or a new /etc/ld.so.preload
    Log source: XCP-ng host file checks, EDR file events
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    | tstats summariesonly=false fillnull_value="-" count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        FROM datamodel=Endpoint.Filesystem
        WHERE Filesystem.file_path IN ("/etc/cron.d/zz-ustar*", "/.ustar5", "/.ustar6", "/etc/ld.so.preload")
        BY Filesystem.dest Filesystem.user Filesystem.file_path Filesystem.file_name Filesystem.action
    | rename "Filesystem.*" AS *
    | eval host=dest, src="-", detail="file ".action." ".file_path, data_model="Endpoint.Filesystem"
    | eval ioc="Persistence files on XCP-ng hosts", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]
| sort 0 - last_seen
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table first_seen last_seen ioc ioc_type data_model host user src dest detail count

